<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Privacy Policy — LifeTold</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Lato:wght@300;400;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

    :root {
      --cream:      #faf6ef;
      --gold:       #c9a96e;
      --gold-dark:  #a07848;
      --text:       #2c2416;
      --text-light: #6b5a3e;
      --border:     rgba(201,169,110,0.25);
      --surface:    #fff;
    }

    body {
      font-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;
      background: var(--cream);
      color: var(--text);
      line-height: 1.75;
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .page {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 48px 24px 80px;
    }

    /* Header */
    .site-header {
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 48px;
      padding-bottom: 32px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .site-header .wordmark {
      font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
      font-size: 1.6rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--text);
      text-decoration: none;
      display: inline-block;
      margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .site-header .wordmark span { color: var(--gold-dark); }
    .site-header p {
      font-size: 0.85rem;
      color: var(--text-light);
    }

    /* Doc title */
    h1 {
      font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }
    .effective {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      color: var(--text-light);
      margin-bottom: 36px;
    }

    /* Intro block */
    .intro {
      background: rgba(201,169,110,0.08);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 20px 24px;
      margin-bottom: 40px;
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text-light);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    /* Sections */
    .section {
      margin-bottom: 40px;
      padding-bottom: 40px;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .section:last-of-type { border-bottom: none; }

    h2 {
      font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
      color: var(--text);
    }

    p { margin-bottom: 12px; }
    p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

    ul {
      margin: 10px 0 14px 20px;
    }
    li { margin-bottom: 6px; }

    /* Data table */
    .data-table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      margin: 14px 0;
    }
    .data-table th {
      text-align: left;
      padding: 8px 12px;
      background: rgba(201,169,110,0.1);
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .data-table td {
      padding: 8px 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      vertical-align: top;
      color: var(--text);
    }
    .data-table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: rgba(250,246,239,0.6); }

    /* Highlight box */
    .highlight {
      background: rgba(201,169,110,0.07);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
      padding: 14px 18px;
      border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
      margin: 14px 0;
      font-size: 0.92rem;
    }

    a { color: var(--gold-dark); }
    a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

    /* Footer */
    .footer {
      margin-top: 56px;
      padding-top: 24px;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
      text-align: center;
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      color: var(--text-light);
    }
    .footer a { color: var(--gold-dark); }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
      .page { padding: 28px 16px 60px; }
      h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; }
      .data-table { font-size: 0.78rem; }
      .data-table th, .data-table td { padding: 6px 8px; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">

  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="wordmark" href="https://lifetold.app">Life<span>Told</span> ❤️</a>
    <p>Every life should be told.</p>
  </header>

  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>


  <div class="intro">
    LifeTold is a memoir companion that helps you record, organise, and preserve your life story. We take your privacy seriously — your memories are personal, and how we handle them matters. This policy explains what data we collect, why, who we share it with, and what rights you have under the <strong>Australian Privacy Act 1988</strong>.
  </div>

  <!-- 1. Who we are -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>LifeTold is operated as an independent product based in Australia. If you have questions about this policy, you can reach us via the <strong>Help tab → Get in touch</strong> inside the app, or at <a href="https://lifetold.app">lifetold.app</a>.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 2. What we collect -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>2. What information we collect</h2>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Information</th><th>How we collect it</th><th>Why</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Email address</td>
          <td>You provide it at sign-up</td>
          <td>Account authentication, password reset, optional weekly prompts</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>First name</td>
          <td>You provide it during onboarding</td>
          <td>Personalising Gethro's messages</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Memoir entries</td>
          <td>You write or dictate them</td>
          <td>Storing and displaying your memories; AI writing assistance</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Photos and audio</td>
          <td>You upload them</td>
          <td>Attaching media to your memoir entries</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Memoir goals (era, audience, tone)</td>
          <td>You select them in the Goal Session</td>
          <td>Personalising Gethro's questions and story generation</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Usage events</td>
          <td>Logged automatically</td>
          <td>Debugging, understanding feature usage, detecting errors</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Contact messages</td>
          <td>You submit via Help tab</td>
          <td>Responding to support, privacy, and feedback requests</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="highlight">Some profile fields are <strong>optional</strong>. You do not need to provide your last name, full date of birth (year only is sufficient), or details about family members. Only share what you are comfortable with — your memoir can be just as meaningful with less personal detail.</p>
    <p>We do not collect: payment card details, or device identifiers beyond what is needed for error logging.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 3. How we use it -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>3. How we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Providing the service</strong> — storing and displaying your memoir entries, powering Gethro's conversations, generating AI-written story drafts.</li>
      <li><strong>Improving reliability</strong> — error logs and usage events help us identify and fix bugs.</li>
      <li><strong>Weekly email prompts</strong> — only if you opt in via Settings. You can turn this off at any time.</li>
      <li><strong>Responding to your contact messages</strong> — if you report a bug or privacy concern through the app, we'll follow up where needed.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not use your memoir content to train AI models, and we do not sell your data to any third party.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 4. Who we share it with -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>4. Who we share your information with</h2>
    <p>We work with the following third-party services to deliver LifeTold. Each receives only what is necessary for their function:</p>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Service</th><th>Country</th><th>What they receive</th><th>Why</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank">Supabase</a></td>
          <td>🇦🇺 Australia (Sydney)</td>
          <td>All your account and memoir data</td>
          <td>Database, authentication, file storage</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="https://anthropic.com/legal/privacy" target="_blank">Anthropic, Inc.</a></td>
          <td>🇺🇸 United States</td>
          <td>Memoir entry text</td>
          <td>AI story generation, writing assistance, duplicate detection (all plans, free and paid)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="https://groq.com/privacy-policy/" target="_blank">Groq, Inc.</a></td>
          <td>🇺🇸 United States</td>
          <td>Memoir entry text (failover only)</td>
          <td>Backup AI processor if Anthropic is temporarily unavailable, configured with zero data retention</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><a href="https://inworld.ai/privacy" target="_blank">Inworld AI, Inc.</a></td>
          <td>🇺🇸 United States</td>
          <td>Question text for voice</td>
          <td>Text-to-speech (Gethro's voice)</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p style="font-size:0.85rem;color:var(--text-light);margin:8px 0 16px">† Anthropic, Groq, and Inworld are configured with <strong>zero data retention</strong> — your content is not stored after processing and is not used to train their models.</p>
    <div class="highlight">
      <strong>Overseas transfer notice.</strong> Anthropic, Groq, and Inworld are based in the United States. Australian Privacy Law (including the Privacy Act 1988) may not apply to your information once disclosed to these overseas recipients. By using LifeTold you expressly consent to this cross-border disclosure under APP 8.2(a). Anthropic, Groq, and Inworld are configured with zero data retention — prompts and responses are not stored after processing and are not used to train their models.
    </div>
    <p>No other parties receive your personal information.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 4A. Sharing -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>4A. Sharing</h2>
    <p>When you create a share link for a memory, that link is accessible to anyone who has it — no account, login, or invitation is required to open it. Links are not indexed or discoverable, but they are not password protected by default.</p>
    <p>Before you share a link, the app shows you this fact directly, and lets you add an optional label (e.g. a name) to help you keep track of who a link is for. We do not verify who actually opens a shared link.</p>
    <p>If you no longer want a link to work, you can revoke it from the Sharing panel at any time — this immediately disables access for anyone who still has the old link.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 5. Data storage and retention -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>4B. Voice cloning</h2>
    <p>If you use the voice cloning feature, a short audio sample (5–15 seconds) is sent to <strong>Inworld AI, Inc.</strong> (United States) to generate a personalised voice model for Gethro or the Story Reader. Inworld returns an anonymous voice identifier — no name, email, or account information is sent to Inworld alongside the recording. LifeTold holds the only link between that identifier and your account.</p>
    <p>When you delete a voice in Settings, or when you delete your account, LifeTold sends a deletion request to Inworld so the model is removed from their servers, not just from LifeTold's records.</p>
    <p>Voice cloning involves recording a real person's voice. Only record voices you have permission to clone. See <a href="https://inworld.ai/privacy" target="_blank">Inworld's Privacy Policy</a> for their data handling commitments.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>5. Data storage and retention</h2>
    <p>Your memoir entries, photos, and account data are stored in Australia via Supabase (Sydney region, ap-southeast-2) 🇦🇺.</p>
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Data</th><th>Retained until</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Memoir entries, photos, audio</td><td>You delete them, or you delete your account</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Account data (email, name)</td><td>You delete your account</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Usage and error logs</td><td>90 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rate limit records</td><td>30 days</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Share feedback from visitors</td><td>Until you import or dismiss it</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>When you delete your account, all associated entries, photos, audio, and personal data are permanently deleted within 30 days.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 6. Your rights -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
    <p>Under the Australian Privacy Act 1988, you have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal information we hold about you.</li>
      <li><strong>Correction</strong> — ask us to correct inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
      <li><strong>Deletion</strong> — delete your account and all associated data directly in the app (Settings → Delete My Account &amp; All Data), or contact us to request deletion.</li>
      <li><strong>Opt out</strong> — turn off weekly email prompts at any time in Settings.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>To exercise any of these rights, use the <strong>Help tab → Get in touch → Privacy question or data request</strong> inside the app.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 7. Cookies and local storage -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>7. Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>LifeTold does not use advertising cookies. We use browser localStorage for:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Keeping you signed in (Supabase session token)</li>
      <li>Remembering your dark/light mode preference</li>
      <li>Autosaving your memoir draft while you type (cleared when you save or sign out)</li>
      <li>Queuing edits made while offline (cleared when you sign out)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No memoir content persists in local storage after you sign out.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 8. Complaints -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>8. How to make a complaint</h2>
    <p>If you believe we have mishandled your personal information, please contact us first using the <strong>Help tab → Get in touch → Privacy question or data request</strong>. We aim to respond within 5 business days.</p>
    <p>If you are not satisfied with our response, you may contact the relevant privacy regulator in your jurisdiction.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- 9. Changes -->
  <div class="section">
    <h2>9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy from time to time. If changes are material, you will be asked to re-accept the terms inside the app before continuing.</p>
  </div>

